WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.836
The best Power BI models share one simple shape: a star.

2
00:00:04.836 --> 00:00:09.973
In this lesson, you will learn the difference between fact tables and lookup tables,

3
00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:14.376
see a real star schema in Model view, and check its relationships.

4
00:00:14.376 --> 00:00:19.880
By the end, you can design a clean model for your own data. Let's begin!

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.670
Here I edit the relationship between Shipments and Sales Person.

6
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:30.700
They connect on the salesperson ID, and the cardinality is many to one.

7
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.815
On the report page, slicers for salesperson and date all filter the same Shipments table.

8
00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:41.286
Why does that work?

9
00:00:41.286 --> 00:00:43.860
Because of the model behind the page.

10
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.259
In Model view, Shipments sits right in the middle.

11
00:00:58.259 --> 00:00:59.904
It is the fact table.

12
00:00:59.904 --> 00:01:04.507
It holds what we measure, like the amount and the number of boxes, plus

13
00:01:04.507 --> 00:01:06.480
an ID for each related table.

14
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.604
Around it are the lookup tables, also called dimension tables:

15
00:01:25.604 --> 00:01:28.187
Sales Person, Product, Geography, and Calendar.

16
00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:31.200
They describe who, what, where, and when.

17
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.675
Put it together, and you get a star.

18
00:01:47.675 --> 00:01:50.346
That is why we call it a star schema!

19
00:01:50.346 --> 00:01:54.502
Every lookup table links to the fact table with one to many, and filters

20
00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:56.580
flow from the lookups to the facts.

21
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.073
Manage relationships confirms all four links:

22
00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:17.620
Geography, Product, Calendar on the ship date, and Sales Person. All active.

23
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.605
A star schema keeps your model simple, fast, and easy to explain.

24
00:02:40.605 --> 00:02:45.628
For your next report, aim for one fact table in the middle, with clean

25
00:02:45.628 --> 00:02:48.140
lookup tables around it. You've got this!

